==Strategy==
Due to the presence of both Malizabeth and Countess Koryessa, it is heavily recommended to use [[Helmet Cat (Special Cat)|Yellow Nyanko Ranger]]'s [[Yellow Strike (Combo)|Wave Immunity Combo]] to ensure your Nyanko Rangers won't get torn apart by constant Wave Attack spam. For Lv. 1, prior to unlocking Yellow Nyanko Ranger, stack up [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cats]] on the peons at the start to repeatedly juggle Countess Koryessa. She's only at 100% strength magnification in the first encounter, which means she's relatively feeble.

For later clears, the abundance of Aku enemies effectively mandates the use of [[Scarf Cat (Special Cat)|Red Nyanko Ranger]], as you have barely any anti-Aku at this point in the game. Koryessa herself isn't very threatening when your Nyanko Rangers are Immune to Waves. Just build up multiple Red, Yellow, and [[Fedora Cat (Special Cat)|Blue Nyanko Rangers]] early on, that way you can swarm her when she spawns. If you possess [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]], he completely permafreezes her where she stands.

