==Strategy==
High Countess Koryessa is much stronger this time around, and she's supported by a cavalcade of strong Red and Zombie enemies. Using [[Helmet Cat (Special Cat)|Yellow Nyanko Ranger]]'s [[Yellow Strike (Combo)|Wave Immune combo]] is basically required to ensure Koryessa doesn't clear the entire field with every attack. Start the stage by spamming [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cats]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]]. You want to keep Koryessa at the enemy base for as long as possible until Zackie Peng burrows. As soon as he does, send out [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to nuke both him and Madam Peng out of existence. Take care of Zackie Peng immediately as he revives too, then try to get Koryessa in a freeze lock with [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]] (this is exponentially easier if you're using [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] alongside him). Green Nyanko Ranger survives an attack from 200% High Countess Koryessa at Lv.34 with [[Red Strike (Combo)|Red Strike]], making it way easier to keep him alive even without [[Ribbon Cat (Special Cat)|Pink Nyanko Ranger]]'s Weaken.

You want to take things slow, handling each wave of peons with [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]/[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]], and whatever else, while ensuring you don't lose any ground. Koryessa's rebounds will mess up any chance at a permafreeze, so keep that in mind. By the third Zackie Peng wave, your Awakened Bahamut Cat will be off cooldown, so deploy him to get rid of the bothersome Peng, then kill him again as he revives. Once the dust settles, there will be nothing left except Zoges and Kaijin Doges; just start spamming Yellow Nyanko Rangers to stall Koryessa and simultaneously chip her down. Once Koryessa dies, it's just a victory march to the enemy base.
